# Dexcom Share credentials for the DexcomG7 desktop tray app.
#
# Copy this file to the location the app expects (default: the
# "credentials.env" file it creates automatically in %APPDATA%\DexcomG7 on
# first run - use the tray icon's "Edit credentials..." menu item to open it
# directly), fill in real values, and keep it private.
#
# Hard-won notes ported from the original DexcomG7 Omarchy plugin:
#
# - This MUST be the actual sensor wearer's own Dexcom G7 app login (the
#   account with Share turned on in that app's own Settings) - not a
#   separate Follow-app/follower account, and not a Caregiver account
#   watching a Dependent profile. Both of those authenticate fine but
#   return an empty glucose-values list (HTTP 200, body "[]"), because the
#   Share API only ever serves the authenticated account's own sensor.
#
# - A phone number with a "+" country code prefix (e.g. +15551234567)
#   works fine as DEXCOM_USERNAME if that's what your account's Dexcom
#   "Username" is under Manage Personal Information.
#
# - If login starts failing with a password you're sure is correct, do NOT
#   just retry repeatedly - Dexcom applies rate-limiting/lockout after
#   several failed attempts in a row. First confirm the password still
#   works by logging into the Dexcom app or myaccount.dexcom.com directly,
#   THEN retry here.

DEXCOM_USERNAME=you@example.com
DEXCOM_PASSWORD=your-dexcom-password
